course: dictionary
lesson: 12008
title: A cheerer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cheerer is a person who cheers. They shout loudly to encourage a team or a player. The ending -er shows a person who does the action, just as a runner runs and a singer sings. «The loud cheerers at the match shouted for our team the whole time.» The clues are loud, shouted and for our team, so a cheerer is someone who is cheering, not someone who is quietly watching.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The loud people who shouted for our team the whole time» still makes sense, so you have the right idea. Always ask: what word would fit here?
explain: The word can also mean something that makes others happier. «The puppy was a real cheerer on that grey day, making everyone smile.» The puppy did not shout at all. It lifted people's spirits, so here a cheerer is something that cheers people up.
fact: A cheerer is a noun. You can say a cheerer or several cheerers.
fact: «Cheerer» means a person who cheers, shouting loudly to encourage a team or a player.
fact: «Cheerer» can also mean something or someone that makes others happier.
fact: The ending -er shows a person who does the action, as in runner and singer.
fact: This is a rare word. At sports days and matches you more often hear «supporter», «fan» or «cheerleader».
exercise: «The loud cheerers at the match shouted for our team.» What is a cheerer? | A referee with a whistle | A player who scores the goals | *A person who shouts to encourage a team | A ball boy who fetches the ball
exercise: «The puppy was a cheerer on that grey day.» What does cheerer mean here? | A grey, wet day | *Something that makes others happier | The fastest runner in the race | A loud shouter at a match
exercise: Which word means a person who cheers? | cheeky | cheerful | cheery | *cheerer
test: Mum was the biggest cheerer at my race, waving and yelling my name. What does she do? | She judges the race and gives the prizes | *She shouts to encourage me | She runs the race for me | She sleeps through the race
test: Which of these is a cheerer? | A quiet librarian reading in the corner | *A fan yelling for the home team | A bus driver checking the tickets | A teacher marking books at her desk
exam: Which word fits best? «The clown was a real ___ at the party, making everyone laugh.» | grumbler | sneezer | sleeper | *cheerer
